WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.161
Cast in metal.

2
00:00:01.321 --> 00:00:06.801
In Benin City, in what is now Nigeria, casters made brass heads for the Oba's court.

3
00:00:06.961 --> 00:00:12.859
The head was modelled in wax, covered in clay, and the wax melted out so metal could take its place.

4
00:00:13.019 --> 00:00:20.774
Each one was made to remember an Oba who had died, and stood on an altar in the palace, so it was never meant to be an exact likeness.

5
00:00:21.474 --> 00:00:22.775
Painted on a wall.

6
00:00:22.935 --> 00:00:32.083
Ancient Egyptian painters showed every part of a person from the side that shows it clearest: the head and legs sideways, the eye and the shoulders front-on.

7
00:00:32.243 --> 00:00:35.726
It looks strange to us, and it was a careful rule, not a mistake.

8
00:00:36.426 --> 00:00:37.819
Naming the medium.

9
00:00:37.979 --> 00:00:40.487
The medium is what a work is made of and how.

10
00:00:40.647 --> 00:00:42.783
Cast metal is poured in as a liquid.

11
00:00:42.943 --> 00:00:44.708
Carving takes material away.

12
00:00:44.868 --> 00:00:46.865
Painting puts colour on a surface.

13
00:00:47.025 --> 00:00:50.369
Naming the medium is the first thing an artist says about a work.

14
00:00:51.069 --> 00:00:52.555
A face has measurements.

15
00:00:52.715 --> 00:00:55.733
The eyes sit about halfway down the head, not near the top.

16
00:00:55.893 --> 00:00:58.030
There is about one eye's width between them.

17
00:00:58.190 --> 00:01:01.255
The ears run from the eye line to the bottom of the nose.

18
00:01:01.415 --> 00:01:04.108
Measure, and your portrait stops looking odd.
